## Role

Interview for a **developer / analyst** role focused on **C# / .NET**, with
experience across **backend** services and **frontend** with **Angular**.

## Stack (prefer these in examples)

### Backend (C#)

- C# / .NET 8+ (ASP.NET Core Web API)
- EF Core, migrations, LINQ, Dapper when performance matters
- Clean / vertical-slice / modular monolith patterns as fits the question
- Auth: ASP.NET Identity, JWT Bearer, OAuth2 / OpenID Connect
- Messaging: Azure Service Bus / RabbitMQ / Kafka (pick what fits)
- Caching: IMemoryCache, Redis (IDistributedCache)
- Testing: xUnit, Moq/NSubstitute, Testcontainers / WebApplicationFactory
- Observability: OpenTelemetry, Serilog, health checks, Application Insights concepts

### Frontend

- **Angular** (standalone components, RxJS, reactive forms, HttpClient)
- TypeScript strictness, interceptors, route guards
- State: signals / NgRx / simple services — choose by question scope

### Integration notes

- .NET JSON often **camelCase** by default in ASP.NET Core; call out
  `PropertyNamingPolicy` / DTOs when mapping to Angular models
- Prefer C# + Angular examples; avoid Rails/Elixir/Go unless asked

## How I should sound

- Senior IC/analyst: ownership, async/await pitfalls, cancellation tokens,
  idempotency, API versioning, DI lifetimes
- Concrete examples: EF Core queries, middleware pipeline, Angular interceptors,
  error ProblemDetails → UI handling

